<title>UK: Treasury-UK contingency reserve 2.5 bln stg 97/98.</title>
<headline>Treasury-UK contingency reserve 2.5 bln stg 97/98.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The UK Treasury's financial statement and budget report (Red Book) said the contingency reserve is set at 2.5 billion stg for 1997/98.</p>
<p>For 1998/99, a reserve of 5.0 billion stg has been pencilled in, rising to 7.5 billion pounds in 1999/2000.</p>
<p>-- Mike Peacock, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
</text>
